    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d103">

                <pb facs="0511" n="497" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v1/pg497"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Glenn, district
                        attorney, to Mr. McCulloch, collector.</hi>
                </head>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Baltimore</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1819-08-24"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi>
                        24, 1819</date>.</dateline>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The inclosed letter was this day handed to
                    me by Mr. Purviance, with a request that it might be transmitted to you.</p>
                <p>I will thank you to take steps such as your official duty require to frustrate
                    the illegal purpose which Daniels appears to have in view, and to let me hear
                    from you as early as convenient on the subject.</p>
                <p>Be pleased to return me the letter inclosed.</p>
                <p>Yours, respectfully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>ELIAS GLENN.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
